3. Opening the plan
The manager and the HR business partner write the plan together. It contains:
the performance gaps, with examples;
between 3 and 5 measurable objectives;
the support the employee will get, such as training or a mentor;
the length of the plan.
The standard length is 60 days. It can be 30 days for employees in their first 6 months, or 90 days for senior roles.
The plan is presented to the employee in a meeting with the manager and the HR business partner. The employee can add written comments and can bring a colleague to the meeting.
4. During the plan
The manager and the employee meet every week. A short note of each meeting is saved in the HR case system. The HR business partner attends a review at the midpoint.

